## Summary

`uoc compare <unit1> <unit2>` raises StopIteration when a unit has empty or missing `knowledge_evidence` mapping.

## Steps / Repro

1. Run: `uoc compare ICTAII401 ICTPRG302`
2. Observe traceback from `src/utils/uoc_api.py:2624` on `next(iter(uoc.data.knowledge_evidence.values()))`

## Expected

- Compare should gracefully handle missing/empty sections and print counts (`0`) or `N/A`.

## Actual

- Command prints header then crashes with StopIteration; partial counts shown before crash.

## Proposal / Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Guard against empty dicts before calling `next(iter(...))`
- [ ] Display `0` or `N/A` for missing sections
- [ ] Add test case covering empty `knowledge_evidence`

